---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
const mailto = 'mailto:partners@rangeway.co?subject=ChargeVia%20host%20inquiry';
---
<BaseLayout
  current="hosts"
  title="For site hosts | ChargeVia by Rangeway"
  description="Explore hosting ChargeVia by Rangeway at an existing retail, fuel, or hospitality property with easy access, useful amenities, and care for visitors."
>
  <div class="title wrap">
    <h1>You bring the place. We bring the charge.</h1>
    <div class="title__aside">
      <p class="lede">For retailers and property owners with a place worth stopping. Tell us about your property, and we can explore how ChargeVia by Rangeway could fit alongside your business.</p>
      <Button href={mailto} chevron={false}>Email partners@rangeway.co</Button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap title-figure">
    <figure class="figure figure--wide">
      <img
        src="/images/cv-retail-1672.webp"
        srcset="/images/cv-retail-640.webp 640w, /images/cv-retail-960.webp 960w, /images/cv-retail-1672.webp 1672w"
        sizes="(min-width: 1320px) 1192px, calc(100vw - 40px)"
        alt="Concept rendering of fast charging beside an existing retail storefront with outdoor seating"
        width="1672"
        height="941"
        fetchpriority="high"
        style="object-position: center 60%"
      />
      <figcaption>Concept rendering. A site&rsquo;s layout would depend on the property.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <section class="band--white" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
    <div class="wrap section stack">
      <div class="split">
        <h2 id="fit-title" class="h2 split__head split__head--wide" style="max-width: 15ch">The place matters as much as the plug.</h2>
        <p class="lede split__aside">Retail, fuel, and hospitality properties can all be part of the conversation. We look at the whole stop, and this is what we look for.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="items items--wide" style="row-gap: 36px">
        <div class="item">
          <h3>Easy access</h3>
          <p class="body">Straightforward to reach, enter, and move around, in a location drivers already have a reason to pass.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="item">
          <h3>Useful amenities</h3>
          <p class="body">Food, drinks, restrooms, or somewhere comfortable to take a break. The right mix depends on the property.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="item">
          <h3>Hours that fit</h3>
          <p class="body">Amenities that are open and accessible at the times drivers are likely to charge.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="item">
          <h3>A cared-for property</h3>
          <p class="body">Clean, well lit, and well maintained, during the day and after dark.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="item">
          <h3>A host who looks after guests</h3>
          <p class="body">Someone who takes responsibility for the property and the people who visit it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="item">
          <h3>A layout that works</h3>
          <p class="body">Room for charging alongside your customers, deliveries, pedestrians, and accessible parking.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section col" style="gap: clamp(32px, 4vw, 52px); align-items: stretch" aria-labelledby="roles-title">
    <h2 id="roles-title" class="display">Your business. <span class="orange" style="white-space: nowrap">Our charging.</span></h2>
    <div class="items items--two items--orange">
      <div class="item">
        <h3>Rangeway&rsquo;s role</h3>
        <p class="body">Rangeway would develop and manage the charging operation and the ChargeVia customer experience.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <h3>Your role</h3>
        <p class="body">You keep running the business your customers know, with the amenities and care that make your property a useful stop.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="body mist" style="max-width: 62ch">Each property needs its own review. Site fit, scope, and responsibilities would be agreed in writing before a project moves forward.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="band--orange" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
    <div class="wrap section--tight split">
      <h2 id="contact-title" class="display split__head split__head--wide" style="max-width: 9ch">Have a place in mind?</h2>
      <div class="cta__body" style="flex-basis: 400px; gap: 20px">
        <p class="lede">A short note is enough to start. It helps if you include:</p>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>The business name and property address.</li>
          <li>What is on site today, and when it is open.</li>
          <li>A photo or plan of the parking area.</li>
          <li>Who owns or controls the property.</li>
        </ul>
        <Button href={mailto} variant="ink" chevron={false}>Email partners@rangeway.co</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
